.TH RP 1 "2026-03-22" "rp 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rp \- repair programs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rp
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B rp
.B init
.br
.B rp
.B inspect
[
.B --verbose
]
.I prompt
.br
.B rp
.B check
.br
.B rp
.B fix
.br
.B rp
.B config
.RI [ subcommand ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rp
is a local-first CLI for turning bug reports into repository-local reproducers
and fixes.
It is built around a small workflow:
.IP "1." 4
Initialize repository metadata with
.BR "rp init" .
.IP "2." 4
Inspect a bug report and materialize a local reproducer with
.BR "rp inspect" .
.IP "3." 4
Run the current reproducer with
.BR "rp check" .
.IP "4." 4
Invoke a coding agent to fix the current issue with
.BR "rp fix" .
.PP
The repository contract is stored in
.BR .rp.yml .
Local runtime state is stored under
.BR .rp/ .
.SH COMMANDS
.SS init
Initialize repository metadata in the current directory.
.PP
This writes
.BR .rp.yml .
The generated file defines the repository verification command and, when
recognized, repository-native test roots.
.SS inspect
Inspect a bug report and create local issue state under
.BR .rp/issues/ .
.PP
The
.I prompt
may be a GitHub issue URL, an issue number, or free-form text.
.PP
The command invokes the configured coding agent in non-interactive mode and
expects a structured result containing:
.IP \(bu 2
a summary
.IP \(bu 2
inspection notes
.IP \(bu 2
a local reproducer script
.PP
Typical files written under
.BR .rp/issues/\fIid\fR/ :
.IP \(bu 2
.B SOURCE.txt
.IP \(bu 2
.B SUMMARY.txt
.IP \(bu 2
.B inspect.md
.IP \(bu 2
.B reproducer.sh
.IP \(bu 2
.B status
.SS check
Run the current issue reproducer.
.PP
This command finds the active issue under
.BR .rp/issues/ ,
runs
.BR reproducer.sh ,
captures stdout and stderr, and writes:
.IP \(bu 2
.B check.stdout
.IP \(bu 2
.B check.stderr
.IP \(bu 2
.B check.status
.PP
Current verdicts are:
.IP \(bu 2
.B reproduced
\- reproducer exited with status 1
.IP \(bu 2
.B not_reproduced
\- reproducer exited with status 0
.IP \(bu 2
.B broken_reproducer
\- reproducer exited with another status or by signal
.SS fix
Fix the current issue in the tree.
.PP
This command:
.IP \(bu 2
finds the active issue under
.BR .rp/issues/
.IP \(bu 2
reads the inspection artifacts
.IP \(bu 2
invokes the configured coding agent in non-interactive mode
.IP \(bu 2
reruns the reproducer through
.BR "rp check"
.PP
If
.B tests:
is configured in
.BR .rp.yml ,
.B rp fix
also requires a repository-native regression test change under one of the
configured test roots.
.SS config
Manage local configuration stored in
.BR .rp/config .
.PP
Supported subcommands are:
.TP
.B config
Equivalent to
.BR "config list" .
.TP
.B config list
List effective local configuration values in
.B key=value
format.
.TP
.BI "config get " key
Print a single effective configuration value.
.TP
.BI "config set " key " " value
Write a local configuration value.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B .rp.yml
Shared repository metadata.
.TP
.B .rp/config
Local repository configuration.
.TP
.B .rp/issues/
Local issue state and reproducer artifacts.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The repository metadata file uses a small YAML format.
.PP
Minimal example:
.PP
.nf
version: 1

verify-cmd: make test
.fi
.PP
Example with repository-native tests:
.PP
.nf
version: 1

verify-cmd: make test

tests:
  - testing/conformance

guidance: |
  Prefer adding a minimal regression test under testing/conformance.
  Choose the most specific suite for the bug, and update the suite Makefile when needed.
.fi
.PP
The
.B tests:
entry is repository-specific.
The
.B testing/conformance
path shown above is only an example.
.SH EXAMPLES
Initialize a repository:
.PP
.nf
rp init
.fi
.PP
Select a local coding agent:
.PP
.nf
rp config set agent codex
.fi
.PP
Inspect a GitHub issue:
.PP
.nf
rp inspect https://github.com/OWNER/REPO/issues/123
.fi
.PP
Run the reproducer:
.PP
.nf
rp check
.fi
.PP
Attempt a fix:
.PP
.nf
rp fix
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR sh (1)
